{"2076540": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Spiritus Astrum", "steam_appid": 2076540, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum, or &quot;Spirit of the Stars&quot; is a persistent, open-world, roleplaying sandbox, with multiplayer support. It features an infinite, procedurally generated universe which players are free to explore without restriction.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solar systems, Stellar phenomena, and planets, are realistically scaled, and players can land and explore, craft, and build at their leisure, using a variety of spaceships, vehicles, and tools.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is designed around emergent gameplay, with randomised NPC's, quests, enemies, and resources. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combat in Spiritus Astrum is optional, the game features diplomacy, trading, and stealth in addition to combat. Conflict between players is not allowed, players may work together to explore or build, but may not engage in coflict. This encourages a cooperative, roleplaying atmosphere. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to customising their characters appearance, players can choose traits and a background for their character. They can be a trader, a diplomat, an explorer, a war veteran, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features &quot;life simulation&quot;, players will need to eat, drink and sleep, in addition to training their various skills.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Skill system is also dynamic, over-training some skills will reduce others, this prevents the &quot;grind&quot; often seen in other games of this type.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Spiritus Astrum, players may live a  true &quot;virtual life&quot;. Players can purchase apartments, land, build homes, and even own their own ringworlds or entire planets! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Players can spend their time travelling the stars on board their ship, living within a densly populated city, or exploring vast worlds alone or with AI or human friends.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is persistent, the players actions and choices matter, and will affect how NPC's and factions perceive them. If the player has a positive relationship with an NPC, they may agree to join your crew, or give you a discount on store purchases. However, with a negative relationship, they may not talk to the player at all!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the future, Spiritus Astrum will also feature the ability for players to create their own stories to share with other players, and the ability to use the games tools to create unique enemies, weapons, and items.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is more than a game, it is a world.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum, or &quot;Spirit of the Stars&quot; is a persistent, open-world, roleplaying sandbox, with multiplayer support. It features an infinite, procedurally generated universe which players are free to explore without restriction.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solar systems, Stellar phenomena, and planets, are realistically scaled, and players can land and explore, craft, and build at their leisure, using a variety of spaceships, vehicles, and tools.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is designed around emergent gameplay, with randomised NPC's, quests, enemies, and resources. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combat in Spiritus Astrum is optional, the game features diplomacy, trading, and stealth in addition to combat. Conflict between players is not allowed, players may work together to explore or build, but may not engage in coflict. This encourages a cooperative, roleplaying atmosphere. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to customising their characters appearance, players can choose traits and a background for their character. They can be a trader, a diplomat, an explorer, a war veteran, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features &quot;life simulation&quot;, players will need to eat, drink and sleep, in addition to training their various skills.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Skill system is also dynamic, over-training some skills will reduce others, this prevents the &quot;grind&quot; often seen in other games of this type.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Spiritus Astrum, players may live a  true &quot;virtual life&quot;. Players can purchase apartments, land, build homes, and even own their own ringworlds or entire planets! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Players can spend their time travelling the stars on board their ship, living within a densly populated city, or exploring vast worlds alone or with AI or human friends.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is persistent, the players actions and choices matter, and will affect how NPC's and factions perceive them. If the player has a positive relationship with an NPC, they may agree to join your crew, or give you a discount on store purchases. However, with a negative relationship, they may not talk to the player at all!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the future, Spiritus Astrum will also feature the ability for players to create their own stories to share with other players, and the ability to use the games tools to create unique enemies, weapons, and items.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spiritus Astrum is more than a game, it is a world.</p>", "short_description": "Spiritus Astrum is a persistent, open-world roleplaying sandbox with multiplayer support. It features an infinite, procedurally generated universe which players are free to explore without restriction. Spiritus Astrum is more than a game, it is a world.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2076540/3aca34fb458b325719b96a6fb8a493a2f0e9539b/header.jpg?t=1788208900", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2076540/04e2406014610457e162f2fcb4373490aec4d734/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1788208900", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2076540/04e2406014610457e162f2fcb4373490aec4d734/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1788208900", "website": "http://www.PhoenixGameDevelopment.com", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i7-6700k or Equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 8 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> nVidia 1080TI or Equivalent<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Network:</strong> Broadband Internet connection<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 15 GB available space</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i7-6700k or Equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> nVidia 1080TI or Equivalent<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Network:</strong> Broadband Internet connection<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 15 MB available space</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": [], "linux_requirements"